# Violent Storm uses the pinned JTFRAME J68 68000 implementation, so the
# fallback FX68K branch is never silently elaborated when the command-line
# define is absent. The actual JTFRAME_J68=1 selection lives in
# ../cfg/macros.def (applied to the Quartus build via
# copy_templates()'s `parse_macros quartus` step), not here: Quartus 17.0.2
# rejects VERILOG_MACRO assignments inside a file included via QIP_FILE
# (Error 125091, confirmed on first real Quartus parse of this manifest,
# 2026-08-18) -- only source-file/derived-IP assignments are legal here.
# CPU microcode assets are byte-identical copies of the pinned JTFRAME/fx68k
# inputs.  Keep them in the project root because both donor $readmem[b] calls
# use bare filenames at elaboration/runtime.
